tab as not copied yet, don''t work numbers out from anywhere else. The tier rules are written up in Robert''s dynamic difficulty deck and in ZOM-42 itself. For when a new player gets their starting tier, where a write-up and the build disagree, go by the build. For which games promotion and demotion look at, write it the way ZOM-42 words it.\\n6. Ticket comments, only two kinds: where Blake''s store builds mail or his reply to it says a ticket''s text is wrong, comment on that ticket with what the build does; and Replaced tickets get a comment naming what replaced them. Every other ticket stays as it is, ZOM-42 and the Not shipped and Editor only ones included, even if its wording is a bit off. Same tickets, no new ones.\\n7. The register goes in the ZM Difficulty folder. Share it with everyone on the tuning session invite: Robert can edit, everyone else comments.", "id": "68daca5871dba40417a00383", "idShort": 80, "name": "Difficulty baseline (Julia)", "shortLink": "IDdFKb6g"}, "list": {"id": "6851a677e090018224fb8c7f", "name": "Oct 21"}, "old": {"desc": "For the Oct 6 tuning session. Julia owns this one. Rules go here once Blake has confirmed what''s in the store builds."}}');
